      </dl>
      <h3 id="_specremotewrite" class="group scroll-mt-20">.spec.remoteWrite[]<a href="#_specremotewrite" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold">Description</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>RemoteWriteSpec defines the configuration to write samples from Prometheus to a remote endpoint.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold">Type</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><CodeBlock code={"`object`"} lang="plaintext" /></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold">Required</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><ul><li><code>url</code></li></ul></dd>
      </dl>
      <Table class="my-4">
      <TableHeader>
      <TableRow>
      <TableHead>Property</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Type</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Description</TableHead>
      </TableRow>
      </TableHeader>
      <TableBody>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>authorization</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>authorization section for the URL.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v2.26.0 or Thanos &gt;= v0.24.0.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />Cannot be set at the same time as <code>sigv4</code>, <code>basicAuth</code>, <code>oauth2</code>, or <code>azureAd</code>.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>azureAd</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>azureAd for the URL.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v2.45.0 or Thanos &gt;= v0.31.0.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />Cannot be set at the same time as <code>authorization</code>, <code>basicAuth</code>, <code>oauth2</code>, or <code>sigv4</code>.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>basicAuth</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>basicAuth configuration for the URL.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />Cannot be set at the same time as <code>sigv4</code>, <code>authorization</code>, <code>oauth2</code>, or <code>azureAd</code>.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>bearerToken</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>bearerToken is deprecated: this will be removed in a future release. <em>Warning: this field shouldn’t be used because the token value appears in clear-text. Prefer using </em><code>authorization</code><em>.</em></TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>bearerTokenFile</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>bearerTokenFile defines the file from which to read bearer token for the URL.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />Deprecated: this will be removed in a future release. Prefer using <code>authorization</code>.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>enableHTTP2</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>boolean</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>enableHTTP2 defines whether to enable HTTP2.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>followRedirects</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>boolean</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>followRedirects defines whether HTTP requests follow HTTP 3xx redirects.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v2.26.0 or Thanos &gt;= v0.24.0.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>headers</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object (string)</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>headers defines the custom HTTP headers to be sent along with each remote write request. Be aware that headers that are set by Prometheus itself can’t be overwritten.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v2.25.0 or Thanos &gt;= v0.24.0.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>messageVersion</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>messageVersion defines the Remote Write message’s version to use when writing to the endpoint.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} /><code>Version1.0</code> corresponds to the <code>prometheus.WriteRequest</code> protobuf message introduced in Remote Write 1.0. <code>Version2.0</code> corresponds to the <code>io.prometheus.write.v2.Request</code> protobuf message introduced in Remote Write 2.0.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />When <code>Version2.0</code> is selected, Prometheus will automatically be configured to append the metadata of scraped metrics to the WAL.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />Before setting this field, consult with your remote storage provider what message version it supports.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v2.54.0 or Thanos &gt;= v0.37.0.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>metadataConfig</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>metadataConfig defines how to send a series metadata to the remote storage.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />When the field is empty, <strong>no metadata</strong> is sent. But when the field is null, metadata is sent.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>name</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>name of the remote write queue, it must be unique if specified. The name is used in metrics and logging in order to differentiate queues.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v2.15.0 or Thanos &gt;= 0.24.0.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>noProxy</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>noProxy defines a comma-separated string that can contain IPs, CIDR notation, domain names that should be excluded from proxying. IP and domain names can contain port numbers.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v2.43.0, Alertmanager &gt;= v0.25.0 or Thanos &gt;= v0.32.0.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>oauth2</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>oauth2 configuration for the URL.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v2.27.0 or Thanos &gt;= v0.24.0.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />Cannot be set at the same time as <code>sigv4</code>, <code>authorization</code>, <code>basicAuth</code>, or <code>azureAd</code>.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>proxyConnectHeader</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>proxyConnectHeader optionally specifies headers to send to proxies during CONNECT requests.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v2.43.0, Alertmanager &gt;= v0.25.0 or Thanos &gt;= v0.32.0.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>proxyConnectHeader{"{"}{"}"}</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>array</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell></TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>proxyConnectHeader{"{"}{"}"}[]</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>SecretKeySelector selects a key of a Secret.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>proxyFromEnvironment</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>boolean</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>proxyFromEnvironment defines whether to use the proxy configuration defined by environment variables (HTTP_PROXY, HTTPS_PROXY, and NO_PROXY).<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v2.43.0, Alertmanager &gt;= v0.25.0 or Thanos &gt;= v0.32.0.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>proxyUrl</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>proxyUrl defines the HTTP proxy server to use.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>queueConfig</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>queueConfig allows tuning of the remote write queue parameters.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>remoteTimeout</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>remoteTimeout defines the timeout for requests to the remote write endpoint.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>roundRobinDNS</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>boolean</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>roundRobinDNS controls the DNS resolution behavior for remote-write connections. When enabled:   - The remote-write mechanism will resolve the hostname via DNS.   - It will randomly select one of the resolved IP addresses and connect to it.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />When disabled (default behavior):   - The Go standard library will handle hostname resolution.   - It will attempt connections to each resolved IP address sequentially.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />Note: The connection timeout applies to the entire resolution and connection process.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />	If disabled, the timeout is distributed across all connection attempts.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v3.1.0 or Thanos &gt;= v0.38.0.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>sendExemplars</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>boolean</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>sendExemplars enables sending of exemplars over remote write. Note that exemplar-storage itself must be enabled using the <code>spec.enableFeatures</code> option for exemplars to be scraped in the first place.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v2.27.0 or Thanos &gt;= v0.24.0.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>sendNativeHistograms</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>boolean</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>sendNativeHistograms enables sending of native histograms, also known as sparse histograms over remote write.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v2.40.0 or Thanos &gt;= v0.30.0.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>sigv4</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>sigv4 defines the AWS’s Signature Verification 4 for the URL.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It requires Prometheus &gt;= v2.26.0 or Thanos &gt;= v0.24.0.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />Cannot be set at the same time as <code>authorization</code>, <code>basicAuth</code>, <code>oauth2</code>, or <code>azureAd</code>.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>tlsConfig</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>tlsConfig to use for the URL.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>url</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>url defines the URL of the endpoint to send samples to.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />It must use the HTTP or HTTPS scheme.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>writeRelabelConfigs</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>array</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>writeRelabelConfigs defines the list of remote write relabel configurations.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>writeRelabelConfigs[]</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>RelabelConfig allows dynamic rewriting of the label set for targets, alerts, scraped samples and remote write samples.<Fragment set:html={"<br>"} />More info: https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/configuration/configuration/#relabel_config</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      </TableBody>
      </Table>
